 "faqs": [
  [
   "How much does it cost to study abroad in Europe?",
   "Less than most families expect. Public universities in Germany and Norway charge little to no tuition even for international students, and at Italian public universities the DSU grant can make your degree nearly free. Elsewhere in Europe, tuition typically ranges from €1,000–15,000 per year plus living costs — we map the full budget for you before you apply."
  ],
  [
   "Can I really get a fully-funded scholarship?",
   "Yes — if you apply to the right one for your profile. DSU (Italy) is need-based and awarded as a right if you meet the income criteria. DAAD (Germany), MEXT (Japan) and Erasmus Mundus (EU) are merit-based with stipends, tuition and travel covered. We assess your profile honestly and target only the funding you genuinely qualify for."
  ],
  [
   "Can I work part-time while studying?",
   "In most of our destinations, yes — typically up to 20 hours per week during term time and full-time in vacations. Many of our students cover a large part of their living costs this way."
  ],
